WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.109 --> 00:00:05.365
- To the point of the small influencers,

00:00:05.365 --> 00:00:07.245
when I launched my book
and it's still something

00:00:07.245 --> 00:00:11.309
we're doing now, what we
do it we go to Amazon,

00:00:11.309 --> 00:00:15.664
look at what similar books
they recommend to mine,

00:00:15.664 --> 00:00:18.115
so it's like 4-Hour
Workweek and Tools of Titans

00:00:18.115 --> 00:00:21.063
and, ya know, all the other
entrepreneurship related books,

00:00:21.063 --> 00:00:23.235
then we go to YouTube and
look up who's done a review

00:00:23.235 --> 00:00:25.213
of these books and then we
reach out to each of them

00:00:25.213 --> 00:00:28.027
individually and say,
"Hey, Evan has this book.

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:28.953
It's about this.

00:00:28.953 --> 00:00:30.642
We saw you wrote about 4-Hour Workweek.

00:00:30.642 --> 00:00:32.835
Would you like to do a
review of this book?"

00:00:32.835 --> 00:00:36.282
And most people just do it for free.

00:00:36.282 --> 00:00:37.698
I often --
- Do they do it though,

00:00:37.698 --> 00:00:40.679
Do they do it because it's
you and you have a big channel

00:00:40.679 --> 00:00:41.910
and they want to hope there's maybe

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:44.043
there's some reciprocity in the future?

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:48.598
I mean, could the average
Joe or Jill do what you did?

00:00:48.598 --> 00:00:49.431
- It definitely helps.

00:00:49.431 --> 00:00:50.786
Like we pick YouTube because I'm known

00:00:50.786 --> 00:00:53.400
on YouTube in a niche, right?

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.432
Like I'm known for
entrepreneurs in YouTube.

00:00:55.432 --> 00:00:58.692
I'm not like known by
everywhere on YouTube.

00:00:58.692 --> 00:01:01.098
But I'm doing it there instead
of Snapchat or somewhere else

00:01:01.098 --> 00:01:03.174
because I'm known in that community.

00:01:03.174 --> 00:01:06.257
So, absolutely, I can do
that in a way that others

00:01:06.257 --> 00:01:08.545
might have a harder time doing it.

00:01:08.545 --> 00:01:10.455
But if you're an expert on leadership,

00:01:10.455 --> 00:01:12.841
like they may resonated
with some of your messages.

00:01:12.841 --> 00:01:15.401
You can still, like your
hit rate won't be as high

00:01:15.401 --> 00:01:17.555
but it's still a viable
strategy to go with.

00:01:17.555 --> 00:01:20.335
And some of them, like we'll
do a shout-out to some people

00:01:20.335 --> 00:01:22.176
on some videos and say,
"Hey, thank you Jill

00:01:22.176 --> 00:01:24.564
for profiling my book, go
check out her channel."

00:01:24.564 --> 00:01:25.808
That kind of stuff.

00:01:25.808 --> 00:01:29.077
And I also offer to be involved
on some of their videos.

00:01:29.077 --> 00:01:30.662
It's like, hey if you
want something from Evan,

00:01:30.662 --> 00:01:32.455
you want an intro, you
want to ask him a question,

00:01:32.455 --> 00:01:34.702
you want something, I'll
make a prerecorded video

00:01:34.702 --> 00:01:36.914
that they can use in their videos as well.

00:01:36.914 --> 00:01:38.591
And so the bulk of our effort,

00:01:38.591 --> 00:01:40.952
I have my assistant spend a lot of time.

00:01:40.952 --> 00:01:43.079
Basically every week
she goes and does that

00:01:43.079 --> 00:01:46.925
and looks at what are the
books that are related to mine,

00:01:46.925 --> 00:01:49.023
which YouTubers have covered those books.

00:01:49.023 --> 00:01:50.822
And then she'll reach out to them

00:01:50.822 --> 00:01:52.690
and we have a constant stream

00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:54.838
of channels of different sizes,

00:01:54.838 --> 00:01:57.984
under a thousand subs
for a lot of them too.

00:01:57.984 --> 00:02:00.047
Creating content, and then
I'll Tweet out the video

00:02:00.047 --> 00:02:02.502
and I'll help promote it and,
like, they get some exposure

00:02:02.502 --> 00:02:04.813
and there may be some
name-recognition with me

00:02:04.813 --> 00:02:06.949
and they may not have any idea who I am.

00:02:06.949 --> 00:02:09.502
But it's been affective in
getting the message out.

00:02:09.502 --> 00:02:11.679
And it's something that
we consistently do.

00:02:11.679 --> 00:02:13.781
- I'm wondering if everyone
picked up on something

00:02:13.781 --> 00:02:16.816
that I did that Evan just
said, and that is he just

00:02:16.816 --> 00:02:20.637
went around and knocked on
a bunch of YouTuber doors

00:02:20.637 --> 00:02:24.183
and asked them to help
him promote his book.

00:02:24.183 --> 00:02:27.078
I can count on one hand, and we've worked

00:02:27.078 --> 00:02:29.214
with hundreds of brands,
how many of the brands

00:02:29.214 --> 00:02:32.572
we've worked with have ever
even thought about doing that

00:02:32.572 --> 00:02:33.655
or have done that.

00:02:33.655 --> 00:02:35.415
They don't have to go
and pay us to do that,

00:02:35.415 --> 00:02:36.589
they can do it themselves.

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:37.647
Now maybe they don't know how,

00:02:37.647 --> 00:02:39.671
it's not that hard to figure out.

00:02:39.671 --> 00:02:41.477
You don't have to hire us
to do something like that.

00:02:41.477 --> 00:02:43.698
But at a minimum I'm thinking
if you got a new product,

00:02:43.698 --> 00:02:46.134
if you're an entrepreneur,
what a great way

00:02:46.134 --> 00:02:48.913
to get the message out about
your product or service,

00:02:48.913 --> 00:02:52.714
even if you don't have a
huge channel like Evan does.

00:02:52.714 --> 00:02:53.946
- Yeah.

00:02:53.946 --> 00:02:55.188
For some people it's an honor.

00:02:55.188 --> 00:02:57.297
Like for some people, I was
the first person to ever

00:02:57.297 --> 00:02:59.658
reach out to them and offer something.

00:02:59.658 --> 00:03:02.851
And then to be involved, to
have me involved in a video

00:03:02.851 --> 00:03:05.757
and say something and to have
a shout-out on my channel.

00:03:05.757 --> 00:03:07.284
You know it doesn't take a lot.

00:03:07.284 --> 00:03:10.252
The exchange could be
we'll Tweet your video

00:03:10.252 --> 00:03:12.933
from our account when it comes out.

00:03:12.933 --> 00:03:14.185
- Or put it on our blog

00:03:14.185 --> 00:03:15.073
or something.
- Right.

00:03:15.073 --> 00:03:17.511
Yeah, I mean, and if you're a
brand, there's value in that.

00:03:17.511 --> 00:03:21.363
And they can say we just
worked with Heinz or BMW

00:03:21.363 --> 00:03:23.620
or whatever even though it was zero cost,

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:26.475
like you can leverage, just
like I'm leveraging my name

00:03:26.475 --> 00:03:28.245
in the YouTube entrepreneur community,

00:03:28.245 --> 00:03:30.004
my brand that's associated with it,

00:03:30.004 --> 00:03:31.232
you could do the same thing.

00:03:31.232 --> 00:03:33.349
People are now, some of
those people are saying,

00:03:33.349 --> 00:03:35.358
"I collab-ed with Evan Carmichael."

00:03:35.358 --> 00:03:38.186
And that makes them look better
for the next things they do.

00:03:38.186 --> 00:03:42.353
So the brand, you can use that
to your benefit to help them

00:03:43.309 --> 00:03:47.476
get more deals and you
don't have to pay anything.

